This repository is a hard fork of duckdb/duckdb-rs (tag v1.10503.1, which
corresponds to the DuckDB 1.5.3 engine). The upstream MIT LICENSE is preserved
verbatim. Modifications introduced by Haybarn:

  - Published crate names renamed:
      duckdb                -> haybarn
      libduckdb-sys         -> libhaybarn-sys
      duckdb-loadable-macros -> haybarn-loadable-macros
    The on-disk crate directories under crates/ keep their upstream names so the
    Haybarn changes remain a thin, rebasable stack on top of the upstream tag.

  - The wrapper crate's library name is `haybarn` ([lib] name). The C API, the
    `duckdb::` C++ namespace, the public headers (duckdb.h / duckdb.hpp), and the
    DUCKDB_VERSION macro are preserved verbatim — Haybarn is intentionally
    ABI-compatible with DuckDB.

  - The sys crate's `links` key is renamed from "duckdb" to "haybarn" so the
    crate can coexist in a dependency graph with the upstream libduckdb-sys.
    Downstream build scripts read DEP_HAYBARN_* instead of DEP_DUCKDB_*.

  - haybarn-loadable-macros emits `::haybarn::ffi` paths (renamed from
    `::duckdb::ffi`).

  - The bundled amalgamation (crates/libduckdb-sys/duckdb.tar.gz) is regenerated
    from the Haybarn engine via the duckdb-sources submodule, which is re-pointed
    at Query-farm-haybarn/haybarn. As a result the bundled build embeds the
    single Haybarn RSA extension trust root (for both core and community
    extensions) and the haybarn-extensions.query.farm repository URLs.
    DuckDB-signed extensions will not load.

  - Only the `bundled` build path is wired for Haybarn. The system-library
    discovery (pkg-config / vcpkg) and DUCKDB_DOWNLOAD_LIB paths inherited from
    upstream still reference DuckDB and are unsupported until rebranded.

  - README rebranded; duck-themed branding and examples removed.

Source for the underlying Haybarn engine (DuckDB as modified by Haybarn) is at:
https://github.com/Query-farm-haybarn/haybarn

The original duckdb-rs project lives at:
https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb-rs
